# How many tests each suite must not fall below. Read by `scripts/check`.
#
# **Why a number in a file** (`docs/BACKLOG.md` B63): on 2026-09-12 one commit deleted
# `crates/ipc/tests/profile.rs` — 647 lines, 27 tests — in the same diff that added
# `progress.rs`, and every gate stayed green for four days. `cargo test` reports what ran and
# never what stopped existing: a deleted test is not a dimmed suite, it is a shorter one, and it
# makes no sound at all. The property this pins is the one that incident broke: **a commit that
# removes tests must not be able to come out greener than one that does not.**
#
# **It counts tests that exist, not tests that passed** — passed plus failed plus ignored on the
# Rust side, the parenthesised total on the Vitest one. A test that starts being skipped by the
# harness is a test that stopped existing for this purpose, and should be as loud as a deleted
# one. A `test-support` skip is a different thing and is counted in its own summary: those tests
# ran and said what they could not reach.
#
# **Machine-independent by construction**, which is what makes a committed number honest: every
# real-data test skips rather than vanishing when its sample is missing, so the totals are the
# same on a machine with the game and on one without. Checked across the two: 992 on both before
# the 27 came back.
#
# **Raising it is a deliberate line in a commit.** The check never fails for a suite that grew —
# that would fail every commit adding a test — it prints the new number and the line to paste.
# The limit of that, stated rather than discovered: a floor nobody raises goes stale, so adding
# two hundred tests and later deleting fifty stays quiet. Closing that needs a per-commit
# comparison, which is CI, and there is none here by decision.
#
#
# **Lowered on 2026-09-20**, and this is the deliberate line the paragraph above asks for.
# Rust −15: the fifteen tests of `crates/design-export` went with the crate. UI −4: four tests
# whose subject stopped existing — the Collection fixture's "pack or synthetic" source, which
# has only one answer now; the wiki index asked for art a second time; and the two that
# guarded `packIconUrl` against the game's sprites coming back. That last guard is not lost,
# it moved and got wider: `scripts/check-no-game-assets.mjs` fails on any tracked picture, not
# just on one the design pack would have carried.
#
# **Raised on 2026-09-20**, Rust +2: the window on T. Eden beating Mother closed half of B20's
# block, and the two new tests are what it bought — where those cells are, and that Mother's
# group of 34 tiles end to end without a hole. Both are sample-free arithmetic, so they count
# the same on a machine without the game.
#
# **Lowered on 2026-09-20**, UI −5. Five tests whose subject stopped existing when the Floor
# screen went from three answers at once to one at a time: `toggled` and its four (there is
# nothing to toggle in a choice of one), and one of the colour map's (a target has one colour
# now instead of three steps with an ink each, because the rank is how full the square is and
# there is no digit left to make readable).
#
# **Raised on 2026-09-20**, UI +8: the eight tests of `shift`, the arrows that move the whole
# drawing one cell under the grid. Seven of them are about the one thing that function has to
# get right — refusing rather than dropping a room over the edge — because there is no undo on
# that screen.
#
# **Raised on 2026-09-20**, Rust +8: the eight tests of B68, which gave the Ultra Secret target
# something to answer. Seven are in `crates/floor/tests/solve.rs` and one in `rules.rs`; all
# eight were written after the code, so all eight were shown red by mutating the three new
# constraints in turn — the dedup in `reached_rooms`, `noPaintedNeighbour` and
# `redRoomForbiddenNeighbour` — rather than by being written first.
#
# **Raised on 2026-09-20**, UI +6: 3.13a's, the responsive frame. Two on the window floor — the
# constant, and the Tauri config agreeing with it, which is the one thing standing between two
# files that declare the same number and cannot see each other — and three on the page thresholds:
# that they are declared in the CSS at the px the constants say, that they ascend, and that the
# window floor falls inside compact. The sixth is not new, it is the old
# `--spacing-virtual-rows-body` test **rewritten rather than deleted**: its subject — a token
# capping every virtualized list at 35rem — stopped existing when the scroll body started taking
# the height that is left, so what it pins now is the replacement, `min-h-0 flex-1` on the box and
# no `max-h-` left in it. Rust does not move: nothing in that sub-project is Rust except two keys
# in `tauri.conf.json`, and it is a UI test that reads them.
#
# **The six entries above are one day's worth, and they are written as deltas rather than as
# `1150 → 1158`.** They landed on three branches at once and were merged here: an absolute number
# on each side is a number measured against a different base, and the pair of them conflicted in
# this file for exactly that reason — twice, the second time with 3.13a, which had written its own
# entry as an arrow and had to rewrite it as a delta to resolve. A delta survives a merge; an arrow
# between two totals does not. The totals below are the ones `scripts/check` counted on the merge
# itself.
#
# **Raised on 2026-09-21**, Rust +4 and UI +2, all of B21. Rust: two on the new shape of a cell
# (the reading it carries, and that reading's JSON), two on real data — the matched window of
# 09-12, and the property over the series that says the online bit belongs to the run and not
# to the day. The two real-data ones passed the moment they were written, which is what a test
# of a measurement does, so both were mutated until they failed and the failures were read
# before they were trusted. UI +2 and not more: eight tests of the bit rules stayed at the same
# count but changed subject — they used to decode a mask and now check that the reading arrives
# intact, because the decoding moved to Rust — and the two added are the probe that says no
# decoder is left there. **Written as a delta and resolved as one**: it met 3.13a's six UI tests
# in this very file, which is the third time the paragraph above has been paid for.
RUST_TESTS=1164
UI_TESTS=749
